.TH ZVM-SETTINGS 1 "October 2026" "ZVM" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zvm-settings \- view, edit, and check ZVM's settings.json
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zvm settings
.br
.B zvm settings
.I .key
.RI [ value ]
.br
.B zvm settings --check
.SH DESCRIPTION
With no arguments in a terminal, open an interactive editor for
.IR settings.json .
When standard input or output is not a terminal, print the settings as JSON instead.
.PP
A
.I .key
argument selects one setting with jq dot notation:
.BR .useColor ,
.BR ."useColor" ,
or
.BR .["useColor"] .
The path
.B .
selects the whole file.
settings.json is a flat object, so nested paths are rejected.
With only a key, print its value as JSON.
With a key and a value, validate the value and save it.
Booleans take
.B true
or
.BR false ;
strings may be given bare or as a quoted JSON string.
URLs must use HTTP or HTTPS,
.B mirrorListUrl
also accepts
.BR disabled ,
and
.B minisignPubKey
must be a valid minisign public key.
An invalid value is rejected and nothing is saved.
.PP
When settings.json is loaded, invalid entries (malformed JSON, wrong types,
invalid values, or unknown keys) are reported as warnings and ZVM uses the
defaults for them without rewriting the file.
The editor marks those entries; saving replaces them with valid values and
drops unknown keys.
.SH EDITOR KEYS
.TP
.BR j ", " k ", " Down ", " Up
Move between settings.
.TP
.BR g ", " G ", " Home ", " End
Jump to the first or last setting.
.TP
.BR Enter ", " i ", " l
Edit the selected value. Enter applies it, Esc cancels.
.TP
.B Space
Toggle a boolean setting.
.TP
.B r
Reset the selected setting to its default.
.TP
.BR w ", " Ctrl+S
Save settings.json.
.TP
.BR :w ", " :q ", " :wq ", " :x ", " :q!
Vim-style save and quit commands.
.TP
.BR q ", " Esc
Quit. With unsaved changes, press q again to quit without saving.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --check
Report every invalid entry in settings.json and exit with a non-zero status if there are any.
.TP
.BR -r , " " --raw-output
Print string values without JSON quotes, like
.BR "jq -r" .
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
zvm settings .useColor
zvm settings .useColor false
zvm settings -r .mirrorListUrl
zvm settings .mirrorListUrl disabled
zvm settings --check
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zvm (1),
.BR zvm-mirrorlist (1),
.BR zvm-vmu (1)
